class Solution:
    def numberOfCategories(self, n: int, categoryHandler: Optional['CategoryHandler']) -> int:
        categories = set()

        for i in range(n):
            found_category = False
            for cat in categories:
                if categoryHandler.haveSameCategory(i, cat):
                    found_category = True
                    break
            if not found_category:
                categories.add(i)

        return len(categories)
```

This solution iterates through each element and checks if it belongs to any of the already identified categories using the `haveSameCategory` method. If it does not belong to any existing category, it is added as a new category. The number of unique categories is then the size of the `categories` set.

